# Project Role: Principal AWS Solutions Architect & Terraform Developer
# Target Architecture: Enterprise Secure RAG System (AWS Option A Stack)
# Stack: AWS (Bedrock, OpenSearch Serverless, Lambda, Step Functions, S3, VPC), Terraform >= 1.5.0, Python 3.12

RULES & CODING STANDARDS:
1. Always write modular Terraform code using standard AWS providers. Split into main.tf, variables.tf, outputs.tf, and terraform.tfvars.
2. Every AWS resource MUST enforce Least Privilege IAM security and encryption at rest using AWS KMS.
3. No AWS service should communicate over the public internet. Use AWS PrivateLink (VPC Endpoints) for S3, Bedrock, and Comprehend.
4. Python code inside AWS Lambda functions must use boto3, include explicit try-except logging, and handle error scenarios gracefully.
5. Provide code in bite-sized, incremental updates. Do not delete existing code unless explicitly asked.
6. Before generating new infrastructure, ensure all variable references match existing outputs from earlier phases.
